apple's new 24-inch imac is definitely a  hit  with its brand new design the incredible  m1 chip  the beautiful 4.5 k display and the  surprisingly thin and light chassis  but now that we spent a good amount of  time with it we've actually found  five issues that we didn't expect when  apple first revealed  the new imac at their spring loaded  event in fact there's  one very important thing that apple kept  secret  until i fix it finally opened it up and  revealed what apple honestly should have  just told us  before we ordered it but before i get  into that issue  let's start with the first one which is  the display size  we already knew for many years that the  21.5 inch imac display  was super small and definitely not meant  for tech enthusiasts  or anyone trying to do productivity work  like video editing  photo editing or even simple  multitasking  so because of that many people went for  the 27 inch display  because of that crazy 5k resolution and  of course  the large display size and we're  actually currently using  two of these 27-inch imacs because the  displays are just  so sharp and large perfect for editing  our youtube videos  so naturally when apple announced the  new 24 inch imac  we thought it wouldn't be that much  smaller than the 27 inch  but now that we've got it in our office  the display is  tiny it's seriously so small compared to  the 27 inch  that it actually really bugs me and you  can definitely see the difference  in our speaker test from our last  comparison video  which you should check out if you  haven't already now part of the reason  why it's so small  might be because of apple's fine print  where they show that the display is not  actually 24 inches it's 23.5  inches so what makes it even smaller  than what all of their advertising made  it seem  like which is a bit disappointing  because that half an inch  can definitely make a difference and to  be completely honest  we were thinking of replacing my imac  pro with the new  24 inch imac since the m1 chip is so  reliable and  efficient and not that much slower for  editing the footage  that we edit on a daily basis but once i  saw the display size in real life  i decided that there's no way i'm  switching to the 24 inch  and we're gonna be waiting until later  this year for the larger  30 inch model but angelica our editor is  actually going to be testing out the 24  inch  to see how the editing experience really  is and she's going to let us know if  it's too small  or just fine for her so if you're not  already subscribed  do so right now to help us reach our  goal of 1 million subs by the end of  this year  now let's move on to the second issue  that we didn't expect to find  on the 24 inch imac and that is the  webcam  quality apple said that the webcam on  the 24-inch imac is the best in  any mac ever which basically makes it  better than the 1080p webcam on  the imac pro but in our experience  it's not always that great in the recent  imac comparison video that we made  we did a webcam and microphone test and  while the 24-inch imac looks better than  the regular 27-inch imax webcam  the imac pro actually looks the best in  that situation  with the 24 inch imac looking way over  sharpened  kind of like they cranked the hdr effect  to the max  so here's another facetime clip i took  with the 24 inch imax webcam  in a much more natural and common  lighting scenario  alright guys so here i am back on the 24  inch imac and just looking at the webcam  quality  you can kind of see noise in my jacket  and this is a black jacket  it is not gray like look how gray this  is and my face is kind of like all  flat and washed out so i don't know  what's going on  but this new 24 inch imax webcam  i don't know what's going on with the  isp but it's kind of bringing  all of the shadows up way too high and  it's just getting rid of all that  contrast  which looks subtle and natural this is  just  really flat so i don't know what apple's  doing but  yeah so as you guys just saw the webcam  is pretty good  but there's something going on with the  software tweaking that is just ruining  the image quality now on the plus side  this is something that apple can address  in a future software update  but it's just a little bit disappointing  that everyone who already bought one  has to wait and hope that the webcam is  gonna get fixed but at least  as you guys just heard in that facetime  clip the microphone quality is  absolutely incredible so i've gotta give  apple props for that now getting into  the  third issue this one really annoys me  about apple's marketing specifically the  part of their presentation  where they said that the 24 inch imac  has the best  speakers out of any mac ever on the imac  spec sheet  they show off that the speaker system  uses six speakers  which means that it should have two  tweeters for high frequency sound  two mid-range speakers for the mids and  two  force canceling subwoofers for the bass  on top of that if you look at ifixit's  recent teardown  you'll see what looks to be two very  large metal plates  built into the 24-inch imac and upon  closer inspection  you'll notice that those plates actually  kind of point to the speakers on each  side  and looking at it from another angle  it's clear that the speakers do  actually port directly into those metal  enclosures  which is a method used in the audio  world to amplify  the volume and the base of the speakers  and if you look at the previous imac  tear downs  they include those same speaker  enclosures which obviously were much  thicker than the new ones on the 24 inch  imac but anyway  the point that i'm trying to make is  that apple marketed the new speakers  to sound like they're way better than  any mac speakers ever made  but now that we've had a chance to  listen to them that's simply  not true just hear it for yourself  [Music]  [Laughter]  [Music]  [Laughter]  as you've just heard the volume on the  24 inch imac  is incredibly underwhelming especially  compared to  the imac pro now i will admit that the  sound quality is pretty good  especially with the vocals but the bass  is  seriously lacking on the 24 inch even  compared to the regular 27-inch imac  which isn't as good as the imac pro so  in my opinion  the speakers on the new imac are  definitely  not the best and i would 100 take the  imac pro speakers  over the new ones time and time again  and in my experience with the 24 inch  imac so far i noticed that i was trying  to turn the volume on the speakers  higher even though they were already  maxed out  which is something that always happens  with windows laptops  because their speakers are always too  quiet and that is something that should  not be happening  on an imac especially after apple said  that it packs the best speakers  on any mac but while i'm disappointed  with them i've gotta admit that they are  still  very great quality speakers that a lot  of people are gonna be very happy with  i just wish that they had a little bit  more volume now getting into the fourth  issue this is actually the one that  apple chose to keep secret  a couple of days after everyone started  receiving their 24-inch imax  luke miyani mentioned on twitter that  the base model  only has one cooling fan compared to two  on the more expensive models this makes  no sense at all because they all have  the m1 chip  and apple showed off two fans in their  24 inch imac marketing  videos they literally kept it a secret  from  everyone even after people were  receiving  their imacs but wait it gets even worse  brian tong replied to luke and mentioned  that the more expensive models  not only get two fans but they actually  get a dedicated heat pipe design  which is obviously superior in terms of  cooling performance  this literally changes everything for  someone who's struggling to choose  between the base  1300 model and the fifteen hundred  dollar model  because what if the more expensive 24  inch imac  actually ends up performing much better  thanks to the dual fan  and heat pipe cooling design well we  decided to answer that question by  going out and picking up a base model  1300  imac and we're going to be doing a very  detailed performance comparison  between that model and our current blue  model to see if there's actually any  difference  so subscribe right now so you don't miss  out on that and now let's finally finish  off with the fifth issue which isn't  that big of a deal  but i definitely was not expecting it in  apple's promotional videos of the  24-inch imac  the color seemed to be more on the  subtle side especially  on the front but now that we've got it  in our office  the blue color for some reason looks  more bold compared to what the marketing  video  showed maybe it's just the fact that  apple used renders or studio lighting  but in our office the colors look quite  a bit darker than we expected  and because of that we honestly wish  that we just  ordered the silver instead which looks  incredibly clean  and thankfully we did pick up the silver  1300 base model  so we could test out the single fan  performance and we're probably going to  be returning this blue one  and keeping the silver one because it  looks so good so i've got to say that if  you're someone who prefers more subtle  or neutral colors  you really can't go wrong with the  silver and it definitely makes it feel  more like an imac compared to the other  color options  so there you guys go those were the top  five issues with the 24 inch imac that  we did not  expect and if you disagree with any of  them go ahead and comment your thoughts  down below  but if you enjoyed this video click that  circle above to subscribe so you don't  miss out on that  bass versus high-end imac comparison  video definitely check out one of those  two right there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one  [Music]
 

