ly underwhelming especially  compared to  the imac pro now i will admit that the  sound quality is pretty good  especially with the vocals but the bass  is  seriously lacking on the 24 inch even  compared to the regular 27-inch imac  which isn't as good as the imac pro so  in my opinion  the speakers on the new imac are  definitely  not the best and i would 100 take the  imac pro speakers  over the new ones time and time again  and in my experience with the 24 inch  imac so far i noticed that i was trying  to turn the volume on the speakers  higher even though they were already  maxed out  which is something that always happens  with windows laptops  because their speakers are always too  quiet and that is something that should  not be happening  on an imac especially after apple said  that it packs the best speakers  on any mac but while i'm disappointed  with them i've gotta admit that they are  still  very great quality speakers that a lot  of people are gonna be very happy with  i just wish that they had a little bit  more volume now getting into the fourth  issue this is actually the one that  apple chose to keep secret  a couple of days after everyone started  receiving their 24-inch imax  luke miyani mentioned on twitter that  the base model  only has one cooling fan compared to two  on the more expensive models this makes  no sense at all because they all have  the m1 chip  and apple showed off two fans in their  24 inch imac marketing  videos they literally kept it a secret  from  everyone even after people were  receiving  their imacs but wait it gets even worse  brian tong replied to luke and mentioned  that the more expensive models  not only get two fans but they actually  get a dedicated heat pipe design  which is obviously superior in terms of  cooling performance  this literally changes everything for  someone who's struggling to choose  between the base  1300 model and the fifteen hundred  dollar model  because what if the more expensive 24  inch imac  actually ends up performing much better  thanks to the dual fan  and heat pipe cooling design well we  decided to answer that question by  going out and picking up a base model  1300  imac and we're going to be doing a very  detailed performance comparison  between that model and our current blue  model to see if there's actually any  difference  so subscribe right now so you don't miss  out on that and now let's finally finish  off with the fifth issue which isn't  that big of a deal  but i definitely was not expecting it in  apple's promotional videos of the  24-inch imac  the color seemed to be more on the  subtle side especially  on the front but now that we've got it  in our office  the blue color for some reason looks  more bold compared to what the marketing  video  showed maybe it's just the fact that  apple used renders or studio lighting  but in our office the colors look quite  a bit darker than we expected  and because of that we honestly wish  that we just  ordered the silver instead which looks  incredibly clean  and thankfully we did pick up the silver  1300 base model  so we could test out the single fan  performance and we're probably going to  be returning this blue one  and keeping the silver one because it  looks so good so i've got to say that if  you're someone who prefers more subtle  or neutral colors  you really can't go wrong with the  silver and it definitely makes it feel  more like an imac compared to the other  color options  so there you guys go those were the top  five issues with the 24 inch imac that  we did not  expect and if you disagree with any of  them go ahead and comment your thoughts  down below  but if you enjoyed this video click that  circle above to subscribe so you don't  miss out on that  bass versus high-end imac comparison  video definitely check out one of those  two right there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one  [Music]


